# Defect 507's class and panel 199's R3, ratified 2026-10-09: a correct
# program whose recursion ends on a callee's `exit`. Panel 199's R1 spares
# it, the call before the self-call being one that may end the program
# (reading R4), and it prints 0, 1 and 2 and exits 0 at every level. Since R3
# clang's `-Winfinite-recursion` is not passed on (`-Wno-infinite-recursion`,
# `selfhost/cli/flags.hero`), the checker its witness, and the `warnings`
# suite holds this build to no clang warning. Reading R1 refused it, which
# is why R4 was built (`calleeexit` in the sitting).
function work(n: i64)
    if n > 2
        exit(code: 0)
    print(n)

function turn(n: i64)
    work(n: n)
    turn(n: n + 1)

function main()
    turn(n: 0)
